export const DOCS: Record<string, string> = {
  "agents.md": "# Rahasya for AI agents\n\nEverything a coding agent or tool needs to use Rahasya, in one file. Raw version: `https://<your-deployment>/agents.md`\n\n## TL;DR\n\n- Rahasya is an **OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions API** for uncensored and abliterated models, served by Venice.\n- Point any OpenAI client at the base URL below and use an API key. Billing is prepaid credit; there is no account or card.\n- **A person has to create the key and add credit.** Neither can be done through the API.\n- Only two endpoints exist: `GET /models` and `POST /chat/completions`. There are no embeddings, image or audio endpoints.\n\n## Connect\n\n| | Hosted API | Local proxy (on the user's machine) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Base URL | `https://<your-deployment>/api/v1` | `http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1` |\n| API key | `nsk_…` | The local key the proxy prints |\n| Prompts pass through | Rahasya's server, never stored, then Venice and the model host | The user's machine, then Venice and the model host |\n\nRead the key from an environment variable such as `RAHASYA_API_KEY`. Don't ask anyone to paste a key into a chat, and never print, log or commit one.\n\nCheck that it works:\n\n```sh\ncurl https://<your-deployment>/api/v1/chat/completions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $RAHASYA_API_KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\":\"gemma-4-uncensored\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Say ok\"}],\"max_tokens\":20}'\n```\n\nOpenAI SDK:\n\n```ts\nimport OpenAI from \"openai\";\n\nconst client = new OpenAI({ baseURL: \"https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\", apiKey: process.env.RAHASYA_API_KEY });\nconst reply = await client.chat.completions.create({\n  model: \"large-v2\",\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  max_tokens: 1024,\n});\n```\n\n## If there's no key yet\n\nAsk the person to do this. It takes a wallet and at least $5 in any token:\n\n1. Open `https://<your-deployment>` and connect a wallet (EVM, Solana or NEAR).\n2. Account menu → **API keys** → **Sign in with your wallet**.\n3. **Add credit** to the API wallet.\n4. **New key**. A daily limit, a total limit and a model allowlist are a good idea for agents.\n5. Store the key in the environment variable your tool reads.\n\n## Models\n\n`GET /models` is the source of truth for what a key may use. Prices are read live from Venice.\n\n| Model id | Tools | Privacy |\n|---|---|---|\n| `large-v2` | yes | Anonymized: a third-party host can read the prompt |\n| `large-flash` | yes | Anonymized |\n| `qwen-3.6-plus` | yes | Anonymized |\n| `deepseek-1017-uncensored` | yes | Private: Venice-hosted, not retained |\n| `deepseek-uncensored` | yes | Private |\n| `qwen-3.8-27b` | yes | Private |\n| `gemma-4-uncensored` | yes | Private (cheapest with tools) |\n| `venice-uncensored` | yes | Private |\n| `venice-roleplay` | yes | Private |\n| `deepseek-abliterated-tee` | no | TEE + encryption |\n| `gemma-4-26b-tee` | no | TEE + encryption |\n\n- **Agents that call tools need a model with tools.** TEE models can't carry tool definitions, so tools are dropped, and the conversation is folded into one encrypted message.\n- **Through the hosted API, TEE prompts are readable on Rahasya's server** while in flight, because that server does the encrypting. For encryption from the user's own device, use the local proxy.\n\n## Request rules\n\n- A request ends after 3 minutes with no data from Venice, or 30 minutes in total, streaming or not. Streaming shows progress sooner. After a timeout or a late failure the key keeps its reservation, so retry with care.\n- `max_tokens` or `max_completion_tokens` must be 1 to 32768. **Always set one.** Without it the key is charged a reservation for the model's maximum until real usage arrives, which can use up a small limit.\n- `n` must be 1. The body limit is 8 MB, and images are sent base64-encoded.\n- The rate limit is 60 requests per minute per key.\n- Of `venice_parameters`, only `disable_thinking` and `strip_thinking_response` are used. Other keys are dropped.\n- In streams, reasoning arrives as `reasoning_content`, and the last chunk before `[DONE]` carries `usage` (not on TEE models).\n\n## Errors\n\nThe shape is `{ \"error\": { \"message\": \"...\", \"type\": \"<code>\", \"code\": \"<code>\" } }`.\n\n| HTTP | `code` | What to do |\n|---|---|---|\n| 400 | `bad_json`, `bad_request`, `unknown_model` | Fix the request. Don't retry it unchanged |\n| 401 | `invalid_key`, `expired_key` | Stop and ask the person for a new key |\n| 402 | `insufficient_credit` | Stop and ask the person to add credit |\n| 403 | `model_not_allowed` | Call `GET /models` and pick an allowed model |\n| 413 | `too_large` | Send less, or fewer images at a time |\n| 429 | `daily_limit`, `total_limit` | Stop and tell the person. Retrying won't help |\n| 429 | `rate_limited` | Wait for the next minute, then retry |\n| 503 | `busy` | Too many large requests at once. Retry shortly |\n| 5xx | `upstream_error` | Retry with backoff, unless the response has `x-should-retry: false`: then the key was charged |\n\n## Local proxy\n\nThe person runs this (Node.js 22 or newer):\n\n```sh\nnpx rahasya@0.1.1         # first run asks for the inference key, with hidden input\nnpx rahasya@0.1.1 token   # prints the local API key\n```\n\nThe inference key can spend the user's credit and move any USDC on that wallet. Never ask for it or read it. The proxy only answers on localhost and refuses requests that have a browser `Origin` header, so call it from a CLI, SDK or editor, not from a web page.\n\n## More\n\n- [API reference](https://<your-deployment>/docs/api): full model table, limits, errors\n- [Integrations](https://<your-deployment>/docs/integrations): opencode, Cursor, Continue, Cline, Aider, Zed, SillyTavern, Open WebUI, LiteLLM\n- [How it works](https://<your-deployment>/docs/protocol): wallets, payments, attestation, who can see what\n",
  "api.md": "# API reference\n\nAn OpenAI-compatible API for uncensored and abliterated models. You pay with credit you added from any token on any chain; there is no account and no card.\n\n```\nBase URL   https://<your-deployment>/api/v1        (local dev: http://localhost:3000/api/v1)\nAuth       Authorization: Bearer nsk_…\n```\n\nAnything that speaks the OpenAI Chat Completions API works: the official SDKs, opencode, Cursor, Continue, Cline, Aider, SillyTavern, Open WebUI, LiteLLM. Setup for each is in [integrations.md](integrations.md).\n\n## Getting a key\n\n1. Open the site and **connect a wallet** (EVM, Solana or NEAR).\n2. Account menu → **API keys** → **Sign in with your wallet**. This signs a one-time message; it is not a transaction.\n3. **Add credit** to your API wallet: from your connected wallet, from any token on any chain via NEAR Intents, or by sending USDC on Base directly. The minimum per top-up is $5 (Venice's minimum).\n4. **New key**: give it a name and, optionally, a daily limit, a total limit, an allowed-model list and an expiry.\n5. **Copy the key now.** It's shown exactly once. We only keep a hash of it.\n\nKeys look like `nsk_` followed by 40 URL-safe characters. Treat them like passwords: anyone holding one can spend that key's share of your credit, up to its limits.\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### `GET /v1/models`\n\nLists the models this key may use (all of them, or the key's allowlist).\n\n```sh\ncurl $BASE/models -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\"\n```\n\n```json\n{ \"object\": \"list\", \"data\": [ { \"id\": \"large-v2\", \"object\": \"model\", \"name\": \"Abliterated Large V2\", \"venice_id\": \"abliteration-abliterated-model-large-v2\", \"privacy\": \"anonymized\" } ] }\n```\n\n### `POST /v1/chat/completions`\n\nStandard OpenAI Chat Completions request and response.\n\n```sh\ncurl $BASE/chat/completions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $KEY\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\":\"large-v2\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}]}'\n```\n\n- **`model`**: one of the ids below. The underlying Venice id (`venice_id`) is accepted too.\n- **`stream: true`**: returns Server-Sent Events in OpenAI chunk format. The last chunk before `[DONE]` carries `usage` on every model except the two TEE models.\n- **Tools / function calling**: passed through unchanged for every model except the TEE models (see below). TEE models also ignore `top_p`, `response_format` and image parts.\n- **Other parameters** (`temperature`, `max_tokens`, `top_p`, `response_format`, `reasoning_effort`, …) are passed through to Venice. You may also send `venice_parameters`, but only `disable_thinking` and `strip_thinking_response` are used; other keys are dropped, because per-request features such as web search can't be metered per token. We always set `include_venice_system_prompt: false`, so the model gets only your prompt.\n- **Output limit**: `max_tokens` or `max_completion_tokens`, from 1 to 32768. With neither, the model's maximum applies, and your key is charged a reservation for it until real usage arrives. `n` must be 1.\n- **Timeouts**: a request ends after 3 minutes with no data from Venice, or 30 minutes in total, streaming or not. Use `stream: true` for long replies: a client that hangs up on a silent non-streamed request can leave the key charged the full reservation. If a request times out or fails late, the key keeps its reservation, because Venice may already have generated (and billed) the reply. A quick 500, 502 or 503 is refunded. When the key was charged, the response carries `x-should-retry: false`.\n\n**Switching from OpenAI:** change the base URL, the API key and the model id; the request and response format stay the same, within the limits below.\n\n### What's supported\n\n| Feature | Support |\n|---|---|\n| Streaming (`stream: true`) | Every model |\n| Tools / function calling | Every model except the two TEE models |\n| Structured output (`response_format`) | Every model except the two TEE models |\n| Reasoning | Depends on the model. Streams send it as `reasoning_content`; `venice_parameters.disable_thinking` turns it off |\n| Image input | Depends on the model; check its page on Venice. Sent base64-encoded, within the 8 MB limit |\n| `n` other than 1 | No |\n| Embeddings, image generation, audio, the Responses API | No. Only `GET /models` and `POST /chat/completions` exist |\n\n### Models\n\n| Model id | Name | Based on | Privacy | Tools | Fallback price in / out per 1M tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `large-flash` | Abliterated Large Flash | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash | Anonymized (third-party host) | yes | $1.25 / $2.50 |\n| `large-v2` | Abliterated Large V2 | GLM 5.3 | Anonymized (third-party host) | yes | $3 / $5 |\n| `qwen-3.6-plus` | Qwen 3.6 Plus Uncensored | Qwen 3.6 Plus | Anonymized (third-party host) | yes | $0.625 / $3.75 |\n| `deepseek-1017-uncensored` | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 Uncensored | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017, abliterated | Private (Venice-hosted) | yes | $0.33 / $1.32 |\n| `deepseek-uncensored` | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Uncensored | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, abliterated | Private (Venice-hosted) | yes | $0.33 / $1.32 |\n| `qwen-3.8-27b` | Qwen 3.8 27B Uncensored | Qwen 3.8 27B | Private (Venice-hosted) | yes | $0.45 / $3.20 |\n| `gemma-4-uncensored` | Gemma 4 Uncensored | Gemma 4 | Private (Venice-hosted) | yes | $0.1625 / $0.50 |\n| `venice-uncensored` | Venice Uncensored 1.2 | Mistral Small 24B | Private (Venice-hosted) | yes | $0.20 / $0.90 |\n| `venice-roleplay` | Venice Role Play Uncensored | Mistral Small 24B | Private (Venice-hosted) | yes | $0.50 / $2 |\n| `deepseek-abliterated-tee` | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 Abliterated | DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017, abliterated | TEE + E2EE (NEAR AI enclave) | no | $0.375 / $1.50 |\n| `gemma-4-26b-tee` | Gemma 4 26B A4B Uncensored | Gemma 4 26B A4B | TEE + E2EE (Phala enclave) | no | $0.19 / $0.88 |\n\nPrices are Venice's and are read live (refreshed every 10 minutes). The table shows the values used only if the live catalog can't be reached.\n\n**Privacy tiers when using a key:**\n- **Anonymized:** Venice strips your identity and a third-party host serves the model. The host can read the prompt.\n- **Private:** Venice hosts the model and doesn't retain prompts.\n- **TEE:** the model runs inside an attested hardware enclave. Through the API, **our server** is the E2EE endpoint: it encrypts to the enclave and decrypts the reply, so the prompt is in plaintext on our server while the request is in flight (never stored). E2EE can't carry tool definitions, so tools are dropped for these two models and the conversation history is folded into a single encrypted message. If you need end-to-end encryption from your own device, use **Truly private** mode on the website or the local proxy (see below).\n\n## Limits\n\nEach key can have:\n\n| Setting | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| Daily limit (USD) | Requests are refused once that day's spend (UTC) reaches it |\n| Total limit (USD) | Requests are refused once the key's lifetime spend reaches it |\n| Allowed models | Requests for other models are refused (`403`) |\n| Expiry | The key stops working after this time |\n| Rate | 60 requests per minute per key (fixed) |\n\nSpend is metered per request from the actual token usage Venice returns, times the model's live price. A limit is checked **before** each request, so one long request can end slightly over the limit; the next one is refused.\n\nYou can edit a key's name, limits and models at any time, and delete it. Deleting takes effect immediately.\n\n## Credit and the API wallet\n\nKeys spend from your **API wallet**, a Base address our server holds the key for (encrypted at rest). It only ever holds Venice credit:\n\n- USDC that arrives on it is turned into Venice credit straight away with an x402 top-up (signed by our server).\n- Venice credit can only be spent on inference. It can't be withdrawn or sent anywhere, by you or by us.\n\nIf a request finds the credit empty but USDC is waiting on the API wallet, the server tops up and retries once, automatically.\n\nYour website chat uses a different wallet, the **inference wallet**, which exists only in your browser. The two balances are separate. See [protocol.md](protocol.md).\n\n## Errors\n\nErrors use the OpenAI shape: `{ \"error\": { \"message\": \"...\", \"type\": \"<code>\", \"code\": \"<code>\" } }`.\n\n| HTTP | `code` | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| 400 | `bad_json` | Body isn't valid JSON |\n| 400 | `unknown_model` | Model id isn't in the list above |\n| 400 | `bad_request` | `max_tokens` out of range, `n` other than 1, or `messages` not an array |\n| 400 | other lowercase codes | The request was refused before reaching the model; `message` says why |\n| 401 | `invalid_key` | Wrong, malformed or deleted key |\n| 401 | `expired_key` | Key passed its expiry |\n| 402 | `insufficient_credit` | API wallet is out of credit. Add credit on the site |\n| 403 | `model_not_allowed` | The key's allowlist excludes this model |\n| 503 | `busy` | Too many large requests at once (one request over 1 MB per key at a time, per server instance). Retry shortly |\n| 413 | `too_large` | Request body over 8 MB (images are sent base64-encoded, so send a few at a time) |\n| 429 | `daily_limit` / `total_limit` | The key hit a spend limit |\n| 429 | `rate_limited` | More than 60 requests in a minute on this key |\n| 4xx / 5xx | `upstream_error` | Venice or the network failed. The status is Venice's when it gave one, otherwise 502. Retry on 5xx |\n\n## What we log and store\n\n- **Stored** (Redis): your user id (wallet address), the API wallet (address + encrypted key), each key's **hash** and settings, per-key spend counters, short-lived sign-in challenges and sessions.\n- **Never stored or logged:** prompts, replies, key plaintext.\n- **Seen in transit:** prompts pass through our server on their way to Venice (see the privacy tiers above).\n\n## Local proxy alternative\n\nIf you don't want anything passing through our server, run the proxy on your own machine. It uses your browser **inference wallet** directly, and TEE models are then end-to-end encrypted from your device:\n\n```sh\nnpx rahasya@0.1.1    # needs Node.js 22+; first run asks for the key from account menu → Local proxy, then serves\n\n# or, as one readable file:\ncurl -fsSLO https://<your-deployment>/rahasya.mjs\nnode rahasya.mjs\n```\n\nIt prints `http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1` and a local API key. Later runs start straight away (`node rahasya.mjs --help` lists the other commands). The site publishes the file's SHA-256 at `/rahasya.mjs.sha256` and shows it in the Local proxy dialog. The file is built from `packages/proxy` in this repo (`npm run -w @pay/proxy bundle`), so you can also run it from a clone with `npm run proxy`.\n\nSame API, same model ids. Point your tool at `http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1` with the local key instead.\n",
  "index.md": "# Docs\n\nUncensored and abliterated models, paid with whatever token you hold. No account, no card. Use them in the chat on this site, or from opencode, Cursor, SillyTavern and anything else that speaks the OpenAI API.\n\n**Using an AI agent?** Give it [the agent guide](agents.md), one file with everything it needs.\n\n## Quick start: chat\n\n1. **Connect a wallet** (top right). EVM, Solana or NEAR all work. Your wallet is your login.\n2. **Unlock.** Sign one message. Your browser derives a private **inference wallet** from it; it never leaves your browser.\n3. **Add credit** from the account menu: from your connected wallet, from any token on any chain (via NEAR Intents), or by sending USDC on Base. Minimum $5.\n4. **Chat.** Pick a model and a mode in the prompt bar:\n   - **Anonymous**: every model. No account, email or card (pseudonymous), but the model host can read the prompt.\n   - **Truly private**: enclave (TEE) models only. Messages are encrypted in your browser and only the attested enclave can read them ([what that relies on](protocol.md)). Click **Verified enclave** under a reply to see every check.\n\n## Quick start: API keys\n\n1. Account menu → **API keys** → **Sign in with your wallet**.\n2. **Add credit** to your API wallet (same options as above).\n3. **New key**. Optionally set a daily or total spend limit, the allowed models and an expiry. Copy it; it's shown once.\n4. Use it anywhere OpenAI-compatible:\n\n```\nBase URL   https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\nAPI key    nsk_…\nModel      large-v2\n```\n\n```sh\ncurl https://<your-deployment>/api/v1/chat/completions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer nsk_…\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\":\"large-v2\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Hello\"}]}'\n```\n\nNext: set up your tool in [Integrations](integrations.md), see every endpoint, model and error in the [API reference](api.md), or read [How it works](protocol.md).\n\n## Which should I use?\n\n| | Website chat | API key | Local proxy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Where | This site | Any tool, any machine | Any tool, on your machine |\n| Setup | None | Paste a key | Run `npx rahasya@0.1.1`, or download one file |\n| Pays from | Inference wallet (in your browser) | API wallet (server signs) | Inference wallet (on your machine) |\n| Spend limits per key | – | Daily, total, models, expiry | – |\n| Prompts pass through our server | No | Yes, in transit, never stored | No |\n| End-to-end encryption on TEE models | Yes, from your browser | To our server, then to the enclave | Yes, from your machine |\n",
  "integrations.md": "# Using your API key in tools\n\nEvery tool below talks to the same OpenAI-compatible endpoint:\n\n```\nBase URL   https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\nAPI key    nsk_…   (account menu → API keys)\nModel      large-v2, large-flash, deepseek-1017-uncensored, …   (full list in api.md)\n```\n\nFor coding agents that call tools (opencode, Cline, Aider, Continue's agent mode), pick a **non-TEE** model. The two TEE models can't carry tool definitions through end-to-end encryption. Good picks are `large-v2` (strongest), `large-flash` (fast) and `deepseek-1017-uncensored` (cheap).\n\nThe configs below match each tool's documented format at the time of writing (Nov 2026). If a tool's settings screen has moved, look for \"OpenAI-compatible\", \"custom base URL\" or \"OpenAI API base\".\n\n## opencode\n\nTested with opencode 2.1.3. Add a provider to `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc` (or `opencode.jsonc` in a project):\n\n```jsonc\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n  \"model\": \"rahasya/large-v2\",\n  \"enabled_providers\": [\"rahasya\"],\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"rahasya\": {\n      \"name\": \"Rahasya\",\n      \"env\": [\"RAHASYA_API_KEY\"],\n      \"package\": \"@opencode/ai/providers/openai-compatible\",\n      \"settings\": { \"baseURL\": \"https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\" },\n      \"models\": {\n        \"large-flash\":              { \"name\": \"Abliterated Large Flash\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 1.25, \"output\": 2.5 } },\n        \"large-v2\":                 { \"name\": \"Abliterated Large V2\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 3, \"output\": 5 } },\n        \"qwen-3.6-plus\":            { \"name\": \"Qwen 3.6 Plus Uncensored\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.625, \"output\": 3.75 } },\n        \"deepseek-1017-uncensored\": { \"name\": \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 Uncensored\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.33, \"output\": 1.32 } },\n        \"deepseek-uncensored\":      { \"name\": \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Uncensored\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.33, \"output\": 1.32 } },\n        \"qwen-3.8-27b\":             { \"name\": \"Qwen 3.8 27B Uncensored\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.45, \"output\": 3.2 } },\n        \"gemma-4-uncensored\":       { \"name\": \"Gemma 4 Uncensored\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.1625, \"output\": 0.5 } },\n        \"venice-uncensored\":        { \"name\": \"Venice Uncensored 1.2\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.2, \"output\": 0.9 } },\n        \"venice-roleplay\":          { \"name\": \"Venice Role Play Uncensored\", \"cost\": { \"input\": 0.5, \"output\": 2 } }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```sh\nexport RAHASYA_API_KEY=nsk_…\nopencode --standalone                     # or: opencode run --standalone -m rahasya/large-v2 \"explain this repo\"\n```\n\nThings that trip people up:\n\n- **File name.** opencode only reads `opencode.json` or `opencode.jsonc`. A file called `config.json` is ignored, and opencode quietly falls back to its built-in providers.\n- **The key isn't picked up.** opencode 2 runs a background service, and that service doesn't see variables you `export` after it started. Start with `--standalone` from the terminal where you exported the key. If you get \"Invalid API key.\" straight away, this is why.\n- **Other providers in the model list.** `enabled_providers` limits opencode to this provider. Delete that line if you also want opencode's own providers.\n- **Spend in the sidebar.** opencode works this out from each model's `cost` (dollars per million tokens, Venice's list prices). It's an estimate. What your key was actually charged is in the API keys dialog.\n- **Only some models show up.** opencode lists just the models named under `models`. The config above has every model that works with coding agents. The two TEE models are left out because they can't carry tool definitions.\n\nThe website shows this exact config, with your key and URL filled in, when you create a key. If the key has a model allowlist, the config lists only those models.\n\n## Cursor\n\nSettings → **Models**:\n1. Turn on **OpenAI API Key** and paste your `nsk_…` key.\n2. Turn on **Override OpenAI Base URL** and set `https://<your-deployment>/api/v1`.\n3. **Add model** for each id you want, e.g. `large-v2`, then select it in chat.\n\nCursor routes some features (tab completion, some agent tools) through its own servers no matter which model you pick. Those parts don't go through this key.\n\n## Continue (VS Code / JetBrains)\n\n`~/.continue/config.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nmodels:\n  - name: Abliterated Large V2\n    provider: openai\n    model: large-v2\n    apiBase: https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\n    apiKey: nsk_…\n    roles: [chat, edit, apply]\n```\n\n## Cline, Roo Code, Kilo Code\n\nSettings → **API Provider: OpenAI Compatible**:\n- Base URL: `https://<your-deployment>/api/v1`\n- API Key: `nsk_…`\n- Model ID: `large-v2`\n\n## Aider\n\n```sh\naider --openai-api-base https://<your-deployment>/api/v1 \\\n      --openai-api-key nsk_… \\\n      --model openai/large-v2\n```\n\nThe `openai/` prefix tells Aider (via LiteLLM) to use the OpenAI-compatible route with your base URL.\n\n## Zed\n\n`settings.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"language_models\": {\n    \"openai_compatible\": {\n      \"Rahasya\": {\n        \"api_url\": \"https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\",\n        \"available_models\": [{ \"name\": \"large-v2\", \"display_name\": \"Abliterated Large V2\", \"max_tokens\": 128000 }]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nZed asks for the API key the first time you use the provider.\n\n## SillyTavern\n\nAPI Connections → **Chat Completion** → Source: **Custom (OpenAI-compatible)**:\n- Custom Endpoint (Base URL): `https://<your-deployment>/api/v1`\n- Custom API Key: `nsk_…`\n- Model: `venice-roleplay` (tuned for roleplay) or `large-v2`\n\nTip: create a dedicated key with a daily limit for long roleplay sessions.\n\n## Open WebUI\n\nAdmin Settings → **Connections** → **OpenAI API** → add a connection:\n- URL: `https://<your-deployment>/api/v1`\n- Key: `nsk_…`\n\nThe models appear in the picker after saving (Open WebUI reads `/v1/models`).\n\n## LiteLLM proxy\n\n```yaml\nmodel_list:\n  - model_name: large-v2\n    litellm_params:\n      model: openai/large-v2\n      api_base: https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\n      api_key: os.environ/RAHASYA_API_KEY\n```\n\n## OpenAI SDK\n\nPython:\n\n```python\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\nclient = OpenAI(base_url=\"https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\", api_key=\"nsk_…\")\nr = client.chat.completions.create(model=\"large-v2\", messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello\"}])\nprint(r.choices[0].message.content)\n```\n\nJavaScript / TypeScript:\n\n```ts\nimport OpenAI from \"openai\";\n\nconst client = new OpenAI({ baseURL: \"https://<your-deployment>/api/v1\", apiKey: process.env.RAHASYA_API_KEY });\nconst stream = await client.chat.completions.create({\n  model: \"large-flash\",\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Hello\" }],\n  stream: true,\n});\nfor await (const chunk of stream) process.stdout.write(chunk.choices[0]?.delta?.content ?? \"\");\n```\n\n## curl\n\n```sh\ncurl https://<your-deployment>/api/v1/chat/completions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer nsk_…\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"model\":\"deepseek-1017-uncensored\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Say hi\"}],\"max_tokens\":50}'\n```\n\n## Agents with a budget\n\nA key works well as an agent's spending allowance. Give the agent its own key with a **total limit** (say $2), a **model allowlist** and an **expiry**. When the limit is reached the API answers `429 total_limit` and the agent can't spend more, while your other keys and the website keep working.\n\n## Local proxy instead of a hosted key\n\nTo keep everything on your machine, use the same configs with `http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1` and the local key printed by `node rahasya.mjs` (see the Local proxy dialog, or [api.md](api.md#local-proxy-alternative)). See [api.md](api.md#local-proxy-alternative).\n",
  "protocol.md": "# How it works\n\nThis explains the money flow, the two wallets, how requests are authenticated and paid for, and what each party can see. Everything here is implemented in `packages/rail` (shared logic), `apps/web` (site + API) and `packages/proxy` (local proxy).\n\n## Pieces\n\n| Piece | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| **Your wallet** | Any EVM, Solana or NEAR wallet you connect. Your login and the source of funds. We never get its key. |\n| **Inference wallet** | A Base address derived in your browser from one signature by your wallet. Pays for website chat. Never leaves your browser. |\n| **API wallet** | A Base address our server holds the key for (encrypted). Pays for requests made with API keys. Holds only Venice credit. |\n| **NEAR Intents (1Click)** | Swaps whatever you deposit (216 tokens, 39 chains) into USDC on Base, delivered to one of your wallets. |\n| **x402** | HTTP payment standard. Your wallet signs a gasless USDC authorization; Venice settles it and credits that wallet. |\n| **SIWX** | \"Sign-In-With-X\". A fresh signed message on every request that tells Venice which wallet is calling, so it can charge that wallet's credit. |\n| **Venice** | Runs the models. Prepaid credit per wallet, OpenAI-compatible API, TEE/E2EE models. |\n\n## 1. The inference wallet (website)\n\nWhen you click **Unlock**, your wallet signs a fixed message (EVM `personal_sign`, Solana `signMessage`, NEAR NEP-413 `signMessage`). The browser derives a secp256k1 key from that signature:\n\n```\nkey = HKDF-SHA256(ikm = signature, salt = \"pay-anything/inference-wallet/v1\", info = \"<chain>:<address>\")\n```\n\n- **Same wallet + same message → same signature → same key**, on any device. Nothing is stored; you unlock again next time. EOA, ed25519 and NEP-413 signatures are deterministic. Smart-contract wallets, whose signatures aren't, are detected and refused. EVM signatures are normalized first (v = 27/28, low s), so wallets that encode the same signature differently still get the same key.\n- **What \"same wallet\" means.** It's the signing key, not the account name:\n  - **NEAR:** an account usually has one access key per device or wallet app, and each key unlocks a different inference wallet. Keep using the same wallet app to reach your credit. The browser warns you if a different key signs.\n  - **Solana:** a Ledger signs messages in a different format than a software wallet, so they give different inference wallets even for the same address.\n- The message contains neither the site's name nor its domain, so renaming or moving the site doesn't change anyone's wallet. The message itself warns you to sign it only on a site you trust.\n- The key only ever exists in browser memory.\n\nCode: `packages/rail/src/wallet/derive.ts` (with a golden test vector).\n\n## 2. Funding: any token → USDC on Base (NEAR Intents)\n\n\"Add credit\" asks 1Click for a quote that delivers USDC on Base **to your inference wallet or your API wallet**, with refunds going **to an address you control**.\n\n- **From your connected wallet:** an `EXACT_OUTPUT` quote for exactly the credit you asked for. Your wallet sends the deposit.\n- **Any token, anywhere:** a `FLEX_INPUT` quote. You get a deposit address (plus QR code and memo if needed) and send from any wallet or exchange. Whatever arrives is converted, so exchange withdrawal fees don't cause a refund.\n- **USDC on Base:** send it straight to the wallet; no swap.\n\nEvery quote must echo back exactly what we asked for (assets, amount, recipient, refund address) or it's refused. Progress is tracked through 1Click's status API (`PENDING_DEPOSIT → PROCESSING → SUCCESS | REFUNDED | FAILED`) and saved locally, so a reload resumes instead of starting over.\n\nOur server proxies 1Click only to attach the partner key, our app fee and a referral tag. It holds no funds and only allows quotes that deliver USDC on Base.\n\n**Fees.** Swaps through NEAR Intents carry a **1% fee** in total, split evenly between us and NEAR Intents. It's already included in the amount the quote asks you to send, so the credit you get is exactly what you asked for. The fee is set on our server, and a client can't change or add one. There is no fee on:\n\n- funding with **USDC on Base** directly (no swap);\n- **inference**: you pay Venice's own per-token prices, with no markup, including through API keys.\n\nCode: `apps/web/src/funding/`, `packages/rail/src/oneclick/`, `packages/rail/src/swap/engine.ts`.\n\n## 3. Credit: x402 top-up\n\nVenice keeps a **prepaid balance per wallet**. To add to it:\n\n1. `POST /api/v1/x402/top-up` with no payment returns `402` with a `PAYMENT-REQUIRED` header listing accepted options (USDC on Base: payee, asset, minimum $5).\n2. The wallet signs an **EIP-3009 `transferWithAuthorization`** for the chosen amount. This is gasless for the wallet; Venice's facilitator submits it.\n3. The request is retried with the `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE` header. Venice settles it and credits the wallet.\n\nThe signed authorization is saved **before** it's sent. A retry re-sends the same authorization, whose nonce can only settle once, so nothing can be charged twice.\n\n- **Website:** your browser signs with the inference wallet.\n- **API keys:** our server signs with your API wallet, right after USDC lands on it.\n\nCode: `packages/rail/src/venice/client.ts`.\n\n## 4. Paying per request: SIWX\n\nEvery Venice request carries a header `SIGN-IN-WITH-X`: base64 of a fresh EIP-4361 (Sign-In-With-Ethereum) message for `api.venice.ai`, with a random nonce and a 5-minute expiry, signed by the paying wallet. Each header is single-use. Venice charges the request to that wallet's balance; when it runs out, Venice answers `402` and you top up again.\n\nSo x402 is for **adding** credit and SIWX is for **spending** it. There is no on-chain transaction per message.\n\nCode: `packages/rail/src/venice/siwx.ts`.\n\n## 5. Truly private mode: attestation + E2EE\n\nFor the two TEE models, the browser:\n\n1. **Attests:** `GET /tee/attestation?model=…&nonce=<32 random bytes>`. The response includes an Intel TDX quote and NVIDIA GPU evidence. We check locally, from the raw quote bytes:\n   - the response echoes our nonce\n   - it's for the right model\n   - `keccak(enclave public key)` equals the signing address\n   - the quote is TDX v4\n   - the quote's REPORTDATA contains our nonce (no replay)\n   - REPORTDATA contains the enclave's address (so the key is bound to this hardware)\n   - the TD debug bit is off\n\n2. **Verifies Intel's signature, in your browser.** The quote's ECDSA signature, the quoting enclave's report, Intel's certificate chain up to Intel's root (built into the verifier), the revocation lists and the platform's TCB level are all checked with [`@phala/dcap-qvl`](https://github.com/Phala-Network/dcap-qvl) (pinned version). The verified report must be the same quote checked above (same REPORTDATA). How it's isolated:\n   - It runs in a throwaway Web Worker that first removes storage (IndexedDB, caches, file system) and network access (XHR, WebSocket, …) and replaces `fetch` with one that can only GET our collateral relay, without cookies. The worker can't see the page's memory, where your inference key lives.\n   - Intel's public collateral (CRLs, TCB info, QE identity) comes through our relay `/api/tee/pccs/…`, cached for an hour, so your browser never contacts a third party. Everything there is signed by Intel, so the relay can withhold it but can't forge it.\n   - A failed signature check blocks sending. If the collateral can't be fetched, the check shows as \"couldn't check\" and the other checks still apply.\n\n   The GPU evidence is reported by Venice's verifier and shown as such.\n\n   **What this does and doesn't prove.** Together these show that the key you encrypt to was generated inside a genuine, non-debug Intel TDX enclave, for this request (no replay). They don't yet prove *which software* runs in that enclave: its measurement (MRTD) is shown but not pinned. So Truly private mode protects your messages from us, your network and the model host's operators; against Venice itself, it relies on Venice running the enclave software it publishes. Pinning measurements is on the roadmap. (API keys and the local proxy rely on Venice's verifier for the Intel signature; the in-browser check is website-only.)\n3. **Encrypts:** ECDH on secp256k1 with the enclave key → HKDF-SHA256 → AES-256-GCM, a fresh ephemeral key per message. Only the user and system roles are encrypted (that's Venice's E2EE), so the conversation history is folded into one encrypted message rather than sent as plaintext assistant turns.\n4. **Decrypts** the streamed reply, and counts any chunk that arrives unencrypted (the UI flags it).\n\nCode: `packages/rail/src/venice/e2ee.ts`, tests against a captured real attestation in `e2ee.test.ts`. Try it with no keys: `npm run verify:tee`.\n\n## 6. API keys and the API wallet\n\nTools like opencode can't sign SIWX messages, so for API keys our server signs on your behalf, using a separate wallet:\n\n```\nopencode ──Bearer nsk_…──▶ /api/v1 (our server)\n                             ├─ key → hash lookup, expiry, model allowlist, spend limits, rate limit\n                             ├─ decrypt your API wallet key (AES-256-GCM, bound to your user id)\n                             ├─ sign a fresh SIWX header ──▶ Venice (charges the API wallet's credit)\n                             └─ read token usage from the reply × live price ──▶ add to the key's spend\n```\n\n- **One API wallet per user.** It's created on first use, its private key is sealed with a server secret, and it's stored in Redis.\n- **Credit only.** USDC delivered to it is immediately topped up into Venice credit. Venice credit can't be withdrawn, so even we can't move value out; at worst someone with server access could spend users' API credit on inference.\n- **Keys** are random 240-bit tokens. Only their SHA-256 is stored. Each has optional daily and total USD limits, a model allowlist, an expiry and a fixed 60 requests per minute.\n- **Managing keys** requires a session: your wallet signs a single-use challenge (5-minute expiry). EVM signatures are verified with ERC-1271/6492 support. NEAR signatures are checked against a full-access key of the account via NEAR RPC.\n\nCode: `apps/web/src/server/` (`keys.ts`, `api-wallet.ts`, `gateway.ts`, `login.ts`), with tests in `server.test.ts`.\n\n## Who can see what\n\n| | Website, Anonymous | Website, Truly private | API key | Local proxy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Our server** | no prompts (chat goes browser → Venice); 1Click quote requests, where it sees your IP, inference wallet and refund address together, and adds our partner key, fee and referral | same | prompts in transit (not stored), key hashes, spend, 1Click quote requests | nothing |\n| **Venice** | your IP (the browser calls Venice directly), inference wallet address + prompts | IP, address + **ciphertext**\\* | API wallet address + prompts (TEE models: ciphertext\\*) | inference wallet address + prompts (TEE: ciphertext\\*) |\n| **Model host** | prompts (anonymized: third party; private: Venice) | only the attested enclave | same as Anonymous (TEE models: enclave) | same as website |\n| **1Click solver** | deposit and delivery addresses and amounts | same | same | — |\n| **Anyone on-chain** | your deposit to 1Click, USDC to your wallet, x402 settlement | same | same | — |\n| **Base RPC provider** | your IP and inference wallet address (balance reads about every 30 s while unlocked) | same | — | — |\n| **Reown relay** | connection metadata, only for WalletConnect QR or mobile wallets | same | same (sign-in) | — |\n\n\\* The enclave is verified as genuine Intel hardware (in your browser on the website); which software runs in it isn't pinned yet, so against Venice itself this relies on Venice running what it publishes. See \"What this does and doesn't prove\" in section 5.\n\nNothing here links your connected wallet to your inference wallet on-chain unless you fund one from the other.\n\n## Failure handling\n\n| Situation | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| Browser closes mid-deposit | Saved state resumes. If no tx hash came back, you're asked to wait or send again (1Click refunds an extra deposit). |\n| Deposit arrives short | `FLEX_INPUT` converts it anyway; `EXACT_OUTPUT` is refunded by its deadline. |\n| Swap fails | 1Click refunds to your refund address; shown as Refunded. |\n| x402 top-up interrupted | The same signed authorization is re-sent; it can only settle once. |\n| Out of credit (API) | `402 insufficient_credit`; if USDC is waiting on the API wallet, it's topped up and the request retried once. |\n| Key limit reached | `429`; other keys unaffected. |\n",
};
